ationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[33,35],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[36,38],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[37,38],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[39,41],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[40,41],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[42,44],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[43,44],"#GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[45,46]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/FASF2S9L","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=2&annotation=NSLLEBH6","line":37},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=2&annotation=PQ9XEJM3","line":37},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=2&annotation=WM5HBR9J","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=6&annotation=3FUKHSTE","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=6&annotation=W8HKQF7C","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 7","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=7&annotation=EW3CW6LU","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LGCRRPJD?page=2&annotation=2SD4U5Q4","line":43}],"metadata":{"Title":"GPT-4o in Nutrition for Inpatients Undergoing Post-Stroke Rehabilitation: Identifying Dietary Errors, Exploring Expert-AI Rationale Differences, and Structuring AI-Expert Collaboration","Authors":"Alejandro García-Rudolph, Elena Hernandez-Pena, Nuria Del Cacho, Claudia Teixidó-Font, Mark Andrew Wright, Eloy Opisso","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1080/27697061.2025.2571878","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Therefore, we aimed to evaluate whether GPT-4o can accurately identify dietary errors in hospital-based stroke rehabilitation menus, analyze differences in AI vs. expert rationale for decisions, and explore AI’s potential role in clinical workflows through a structured collaboration framework.GPT-4o’s dietary compliance classifications were assessed using a structured 0-error, 1-error, and 2+ error framework, with expert dietitians as ground-truth in a rehabilitation hospital nutrition department, where expert dietitians selected menus from existing clinical practices for inpatients on specialized diets. AI-expert agreement, overall accuracy, sensitivity, and specificity in dietary error classification were assessed","Findings":"Thematic analysis revealed GPT-4o followed strict rule-based interpretations, whereas dietitians incorporated patient tolerance and food preparation considerations.items), discrepancies were found in 26 menus, representing 9.8% of cases.  Despite these discrepancies, GPT-4o achieved an overall classification accuracy of 92.8%, correctly identifying dietary compliance or violations in the majority of casDespite these discrepancies, GPT-4o demonstrated an overall strong agreement with expert dietitians, with Cohen’s Kappa of 0.892 (95% CI: 0.845–0.939, p<0.001), indicating high reliability in dietary error identificatiologic (1): AI Lacks Contextual Flexibility in Applying Dietary Guidelines (2), AI Prioritizes Nutritional Absolutes Over Clinical Meal Planning (3), AI Overestimates Allergen and Safety Risks, and (4) AI Misinterprets Textural Considerations for Dysphagia Patients.","Conclusions":"GPT-4o demonstrated high accuracy but over-flagged violations, supporting its role as a prescreening tool with expert collaboration.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"prompt var  dyt kar var  dyt=ai çıkmış"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"ktvcbd","at":1774939758100},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/garcia-rudolphGPT4oNutritionInpatients2025b.md"},
